<Post title="Guaranteed delivery: paper and sources" description="Exact maxima and explicit attaining constructions, with the research manuscript, reproducible certificates, sources and Lean development." updated={release.publication_date}>
  <p><a href="/cop-prisoner/">Exact-count overview</a> · <a href="/cop-prisoner/proofs/">Classification proofs</a> · <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/">Lean coverage</a> · <a href="/cop-prisoner/delivery-time/">Delivery-time companion</a></p>
  <p><strong>Guaranteed indirect delivery in directed networks</strong><br/>Exact maxima and explicit attaining constructions.</p>
  <p>This is a {release.pages}-page research checkpoint with {release.figures} figures. It determines the exact maximum <i>M(n,m)</i> for every <i>n ≥ 1</i> and <i>0 ≤ m ≤ n(n − 1)</i>, together with concrete adjacency rules, a specified attaining composition whose parameters are determined from <i>(n,m)</i>, or a certified listed finite graph. <strong>The exact-count classification and its explicit attainers are complete.</strong> Four budget regimes cover every order from twelve, and full finite tables cover orders one through eleven. Vertex-only and arc-only maxima follow as consequences. The manuscript has not been submitted to arXiv.</p>
  <p>The uniform main-interval formula <i>M(n,m) = n(n − 1) − m</i> holds for every <i>n ≥ 12</i> and <i>2n ≤ m ≤ n(n − 3)</i>, with a sharp order threshold. Fixed staged certificates, six-offset circles and a reduced hub interface connect smaller orders to the retained infinite constructions. The <a href="/cop-prisoner/proofs/#completion-of-the-finite-sparse-budgets">finite sparse-budget chapter</a> supplies the exact arrow-only values from twelve through twenty-one. The <a href="/cop-prisoner/proofs/#complete-tables-through-eleven-vertices">complete finite tables</a> give every smaller-host value, including all of the eight-, nine- and ten-vertex rows. At order eleven, budgets 22, 23 and 24 have values 79, 78 and 79.</p>
  <p>The <a href="/cop-prisoner/#explicit-constructions">explicit-construction inventory</a> is separate from numerical coverage. Its family-by-family audit identifies a direct recipe or certified listed graph for every resource pair. This conclusion rests on the actual recipes and their parameters, in addition to the value proofs. Conditional and probabilistic results retain their stronger stated properties and their original proof boundaries.</p>
  <p>The final dense staircase has sharp threshold eleven and explicit attaining graphs within four moves throughout that range. The earlier two-move guarantee still covers the complete band from order sixteen. Smaller finite exceptions retain their own bounds, including five moves at nine stations and 55 arrows. Delivery-time optimization is retained in a separate <a href="/cop-prisoner/delivery-time/">parked companion</a>, with proved and partial results distinguished.</p>
