  <h2>Delivery-time companion</h2>
  <p>The separate {release.companions.delivery_time.pages}-page companion preserves the proved delivery-time bounds and explicitly partial constructions. Read it <a href="/cop-prisoner/delivery-time/">on the website</a>, download the <a href="/cop-prisoner/delivery-time-companion.pdf">companion PDF</a>, or inspect the <a href="/cop-prisoner/delivery-time-source.zip">LaTeX source archive</a>. Further work on these time-optimization questions is parked.</p>
  <p>The <a href="/cop-prisoner/lean/">Lean coverage map</a> states which results are formalized in the existing twelve modules. They include generic robust-layer and staged-envelope semantics: supplied decreasing ranks and safe-entry hypotheses imply actual delivery, including ranks depending on both player positions. The concrete circle arithmetic, guide-code conditions, support reductions and safe-root transfers have ordinary proofs; the large finite stages and complete finite exclusions have independent external checks. The approved <code>research/small-case-results.json</code> registry in the research archive indexes the literal graphs, stages and upper proofs. The complete classification is not claimed as a Lean theorem. The <a href="#evidence-guide">evidence and replay guide</a> below distinguishes independent game replay, reviewed enumeration coverage and any separately implemented graph enumeration.</p>
